{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-37564-r4511535","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Binagoongan (Sautéed Pork with Shrimp Paste)","sourcePageId":37564,"sourceRevision":"4511535","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-17T14:57:55Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Binagoongan%20(Saut%C3%A9ed%20Pork%20with%20Shrimp%20Paste)&oldid=4511535","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:24:43.580Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Filipino recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using bagoong alamang","Category:Recipes using bitter melon","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using onion","Category:Recipes using pork","Category:Recipes using shrimp","Category:Recipes using vinegar","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"5811747a8e495ed97b8f5863518197e0d7b9976a7732ce5ebfc8e605ca37b2cd","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Pork recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n| Image = [[File:4336Cuisine and foods of Baliuag, Bulacan 08.jpg|300px]]\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of the Philippines|Cuisine of the Philippines]]\n\n'''Binagoongan''' is a Filipino cooking process consisting of vegetables (most notably water spinach) or meat (usually pork, but can also be chicken or beef) sautéed or braised in bagoong alamang (shrimp paste), garlic, black peppercorns, and bay leaves. Some recipes also add pineapples, chilis, or coconut cream to balance the flavors. The dish is characteristically quite salty with a strong umami flavor, which is why it is always paired with white rice and never eaten on its own. It is very similar to pinatisan which is cooked with patis (fish sauce), one of the by-products of fermenting bagoong.\n\nSautéed pork from the [[Cookbook:Cuisine of the Philippines|Philippines]].\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n*1 [[Cookbook:Pound|lb]] [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]], cut into pieces\n*½ lb of [[cookbook:Shrimp|baby shrimp]] \n*½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] of [[cookbook:bitter melon|bitter melon]]\n*¼ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Oil|oil]] \n*½ head [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], crushed \n*1 [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]] thinly \n*1 large [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomato]], sliced \n*½ cup [[Cookbook:Bagoong alamang|bagoong alamang]] \n*½ cup [[Cookbook:Vinegar|vinegar]] \n*2 cups water\n\n==Procedure==\n\n#[[cookbook:pan fry|Fry]] pork pieces in hot oil. \n#[[cookbook:Sauté|Sauté]] garlic, onions and tomatoes after pork has browned.\n#Add shrimp.\n#Add the rest of the ingredients and let [[cookbook:simmer|simmer]] until pork is tender. If desired, let water reduce. \n#Serve with [[Cookbook:Rice|rice]].\n\n[[Category:Recipes using pork]]\n[[Category:Recipes using shrimp]]\n[[Category:Filipino recipes]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bagoong alamang]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bitter melon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vinegar]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Binagoongan (Sautéed Pork with Shrimp Paste)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","n